[2026-09-12 ~23:00] MET-FORCING BIAS CHECK (custom_py/met_bias/, full-year
  hourly vs BOM stations; summary CSV there):
  - ANNUAL air-T bias ~0 for BOTH forcings (WRF-2021 -0.13..+0.05; BARRA-SUB
    2013 -0.28..-0.10) — the simple "WRF is warm" story does not hold
    annually (the hosted page's +1.76 was a Jan-2022 fortnight; our Jan-2021
    WRF is actually -1.7..-2.2 COLD at GI/Rottnest).
  - SEASONAL structure is the story: WRF-2021 runs +0.7..+1.15 degC WARM
    Apr-Aug at Garden Is/Rottnest then COLD Nov-Jan; BARRA-SUB 2013's warm
    season lean is half that (<=+0.6). Water T integrates the flux -> the
    accumulated Apr-Aug surplus surfaces as the Jul-Oct water warm offset
    (TransectA: Jul +0.83 .. Oct +1.18) and the Nov-Dec cold bias pulls Dec
    back to ~0 — the 2021 pattern matches a lagged integral of WRF's
    seasonal air-T bias. WRF GI wind also +1.0 m/s (partial evaporative
    offset). BARRA-C2 (4-5 km counterfactual): noisy/warm at land stations,
    not an obvious upgrade at the coast.
  => 1.8 physics stays (validated on the BARRA-forced 1991+2013, both
  improved); candidate remedies for WRF years: seasonal air-T bias
  correction of WRF, or a BARRA-C2-forced 2021 sensitivity run (data on
  store covers 20201101-20220331) for definitive attribution.

